{
  "id": "faber-hymns",
  "cover": "classic",
  "name": {
    "en-US": "Hymns",
    "pt-BR": "Hinos"
  },
  "author": {
    "en-US": "Fr. Frederick William Faber",
    "pt-BR": "Pe. Frederick William Faber"
  },
  "description": {
    "en-US": "The hundred and fifty hymns of Faber, as he collected them in 1862 from his Jesus and Mary (1849) and the Oratory Hymns (1854): God and the Holy Trinity, the Sacred Humanity of Jesus, Our Lady and St. Joseph, the angels and saints, the sacraments, the faith and the spiritual life, miscellaneous hymns and the last things. They include \"Faith of our Fathers\", \"There's a wideness in God's mercy\" and \"My God, how wonderful Thou art\".",
    "pt-BR": "Os cento e cinquenta hinos de Faber, como os reuniu em 1862 a partir de Jesus and Mary (1849) e dos Oratory Hymns (1854): Deus e a Santíssima Trindade, a Sagrada Humanidade de Jesus, Nossa Senhora e São José, os anjos e santos, os sacramentos, a fé e a vida espiritual, hinos diversos e as últimas coisas. Entre eles estão \"Faith of our Fathers\", \"There's a wideness in God's mercy\" e \"My God, how wonderful Thou art\"."
  },
  "composed": "1849-1862",
  "languages": [
    "en-US"
  ],
  "work": "faber/hymns",
  "editions": {
    "en-US": {
      "editor": "Fr. Frederick William Faber (Father Faber's Hymns, New York: P. J. Kenedy / Murphy)",
      "year": 1880
    }
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "language": "en-US",
      "url": "https://archive.org/details/hymns00faberich",
      "edition": "Father Faber's Hymns (the complete 150 hymns, 1880 printing), Internet Archive full-text OCR.",
      "description": "The 150 hymns, one chapter each, grouped in the seven parts of the collection; stanza numbers, running heads and page numbers are dropped, and the hard line breaks of the verse are kept. The editor's introduction, the contents and the index of first lines are left out. The OCR is uncorrected apart from spacing, and isolated slips remain. Raw OCR in sources/en-US-originals/.",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "Faber died in 1863 and the hymns first appeared in 1849-1862, so the text is public domain."
    }
  ],
